 "text": "Border Ag and Energy\nSkip to content\nHome\nAbout Overview\nTeam\nCareers\nLocations\nDAP\nScholarship\nMarkets Cash Bids\nFutures Quotes\nDTN Insights DTN News\nWeather\nHelpful Links\nDiscount Schedules\nMy Grower\nBorder ag & Energy\nCash Bids\nFutures\nWeather\nNews\nAnnouncements\n9/8/26 Falling Numbers in Spring Wheat have become an issue. See statement under discounts for more information.\noperating Hours\nHarvest Hours when the weather cooperates.\nBottineau and Russell now have space for corn.\nBottineau will be open for dumping corn Noon to 4PM on 11/8/26\nCall the location for hours and what moistures they are currently dumping.\nOther locations call to confirm hours.\nOffice: Monday-Friday from 8:00am to 5:00pm\nNormal receiving hours: Monday-Friday from 8:00am to 5:00pm\nLinks to the new app at the bottom of the page.\nJob Openings\nNew Job Opening listed. Look under the About Us tab and Careers.\nFacility Updates\nRussell has limited spring wheat room, can only accept spring wheat with falling numbers of 250 or better.\nBottineau Bulk Fuel Deliveries\nWe have P-40 winter diesel fuel in stock and at the pump in Bottineau. Newburg still has #2 fuel at the pumps. For Bulk and Tanker Fuel deliveries of diesel fuel and gas, call Virgil Borman at 701-721-1181 or Brandon at the main office.\nNewburg Repair Shop Services\nHeavy Duty Truck and Trailer repair as well light duty automotive and tires at the shop in Newburg. Call Scott to get scheduled at 272-6158.\nLocation Discounts\nKramer, Lansford, Souris, and Westhope have a 10 cent discount on Wheat and Soybean pricing as of 01/01/26.\nSpring Wheat Specifications\nSpring Wheat Bids are 300 Falling Numbers Or Better and 25 DHV or Better.\nDelayed Price Storage Rates\nDelayed Priced contracts as of 07/01/26. New Delivery contracts only. Customers will have 30 days free from delivery after 30 days it will start charges back to day of delivery. Contracts need to be signed when done with delivery. Please advise the office when done.\nSpring Wheat: 8 cents/bu per month\nSoybeans: 8 cents/bu per month\nWinter Wheat: CASH\nCorn: CASH\nDurum: CASH\nCanola: CASH\nALL COMMODITIES SUBJECT TO CASH AT ANYTIME\nCondo Bushels\nSpring Wheat, Soybeans, and #2 Yellow Corn (54# TW or better, Less than 3%BCFM) are the only commodities currently available for the condo. Condo bushels can be delivered to all locations but are subject to the pricing of that facility.\nSpring Wheat Protein Scale\nEffective 08/05/26:\nProtein Level\n| Scale\n|\nOver 14.0 (16.0 max)\n| +.02 each 1/5\n|\nBelow 14.0 down to 12.0\n| -.02 each 1/5\n|\nCash Bids\nREFRESH\nFutures\nView More\nCORN\nDescription | Last | Open | Close | Change | Last Update | High | Low | Chart |\nDecember 2026 | 445'4 | 442'2 | -- | 3'0 | November 12, 2026 at 07:54 PM | 445'6 | 441'6 | |\nMarch 2027 | 457'6 | 454'6 | -- | 3'0 | November 12, 2026 at 07:54 PM | 458'0 | 454'0 | |\nMay 2027 | 465'4 | 462'4 | -- | 2'6 | November 12, 2026 at 07:46 PM | 465'4 | 461'6 | |\nJuly 2027 | 472'0 | 469'2 | -- | 2'6 | November 12, 2026 at 07:40 PM | 472'0 | 468'6 | |\nSeptember 2027 | 466'6 | 464'0 | -- | 2'6 | November 12, 2026 at 07:27 PM | 466'6 | 464'0 | |\nWHEAT\nDescription | Last | Open | Close | Change | Last Update | High | Low | Chart |\nDecember 2026 | 589'6 | 582'6 | -- | 5'4 | November 12, 2026 at 07:54 PM | 590'0 | 582'0 | |\nMarch 2027 | 605'0 | 598'0 | -- | 5'6 | November 12, 2026 at 07:54 PM | 605'2 | 597'0 | |\nMay 2027 | 611'0 | 604'4 | -- | 6'0 | November 12, 2026 at 07:54 PM | 611'0 | 603'2 | |\nJuly 2027 | 616'2 | 609'4 | -- | 5'4 | November 12, 2026 at 07:52 PM | 616'4 | 609'0 | |\nSeptember 2027 | 627'6 | 621'0 | -- | 5'6 | November 12, 2026 at 07:49 PM | 627'6 | 620'4 | |\nHARD RED SPRING WHEAT MPLS\nDescription | Last | Open | Close | Change | Last Update | High | Low | Chart |\nDecember 2026 | 6.2325 | 6.2200 | -- | 0.0050 | November 12, 2026 at 07:33 PM | 6.2475 | 6.2100 | |\nMarch 2027 | 6.3700 | 6.3600 | -- | 